Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:07:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: city programs specialised by material for Adreno GPUs

The city's fragment program handles every material in one function, picked at run time by
mat.mode, with ~230 more branches for the diagnostics views (MCLA_DEBUG_VIEW). Turnip's
compiler makes ~21 000 instructions of it at the register limit (48 registers, 4 waves),
and the city pass took 370 ms a frame on an Adreno 740.

Without MCLA_DEBUG_VIEW the program is built with the diagnostics test fixed to 0, and each
(pipeline, material) pair gets a pipeline of its own with the material fixed (2 500 - 5 500
instructions, 16 - 24 registers, 8 - 12 waves). They are built on worker threads on first
use; the shared pipeline draws until then. MCLA_CITY_SPEC=0 keeps the shared pipelines only.
